  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\n\nThe Pearson Cup: Indian 19th Century Hunting Scene Engraved Silver Bowl\n\n'ELLO\n\n19th Century Indian silver bowl, decorated with dancers, court and hunting scenes. Cups like this often awarded to officers during inter-regimental competitions in areas such as hunting and shooting. The cup measures 10 inches at the rim and weighs 76 ounces.\n\nPrevious:\nBison Hoof Double Snuff Box, made in Sheffield in 1876.\nNext:\nPrivate H. Lines’ Personal Razor (Boer War)\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
